# EVERY CONSTRUCTION HERE IS CHOSEN FOR SEPARABILITY, since a classifier
# answers stretch FIRST when all children span (docs/deferred.md):
#   - column@centered's children have DIFFERENT natural widths, so
#     coinciding centers can only be center.
#   - row#0's TALL no-baseline image (2x64) is what stops a hug-height
#     row collapsing the four modes into the tolerance (docs/traps.md —
#     on macOS baseline placement equals center).
#   - column@fitcol is grow=1 AND align=stretch, the shape that drew a
#     third of itself with every model observable green; its two asserts
#     hold the grow half and the stretch half separately.
expect label#0 "align probe"
expect_aligned column@root "stretch"
expect_aligned column@centered "center"
expect_aligned row#0 "baseline"
expect_aligned column@fitcol "stretch"
expect_fills column@fitcol
